//--------------------------------------------------------------------
// ---- Jokers Explained -----
//--------------------------------------------------------------------
D = Single line
E = questionable -  Becuase conflict with multi-line and compparatives (less/more than, not/equal to)
TKBS {Notes}
	usual game dev values are 0,1,2 (greyed or default, on or true, off or false) - 0,255 (true, false) - 0-65536(limit)
	HEX for 255, True Boolean == FF, unfortunately FFFF == 65535, 65536 = 1 0000(hex)

	Press a button will usually switch a 00 -> FF at some byte.

OrionSR explanation:
	Multi-Line Joker (E). Execute 0x006 lines IF L1+UP (FBEF) is pressed (00700942):
	E006FBEF 00700942 (NTSC)

ISSUES:
	OrionSR's explanation & example conflicts with the tested working examples
	The issue is that using e.g. "6" for execute 6 lines, is the same bit as where we use 1 for equal to, 2 for less than comparisons etc.
	So how to write
	Execute 12 Lines IF value at address == FFFF

Other Methods:
	UNKNOWN assumed to be the above method, but only game method - doesn't explain original code creators who used IO/Port methods and software used.
